<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kumukh</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Kumukh is a large mountain village in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lak">Lak</a> district of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dagestan">Dagestan</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a>, the historic centre of the Lak people. One of the earliest centres of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/islam">Islam</a> in mountainous Dagestan, it was the seat of the Kazikumukh shamkhals and, from the 17th century, of the khans of Kazikumukh. Its old mosque dates in part from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/middle-ages">medieval period</a>.</p></div>
